[Music]  so day one of the middle split challenge  so yeah i used to be able to do the  middle split actually  like two years ago so kind of before  corona because i danced a lot so i  practiced a lot of stretching and  everything but the last  two years i guess i haven't really done  any stretching at all except for one  week  one day a week a little bit of yoga  and that's it and that's not enough to  keep up your flexibility so i'm gonna  try this week to see if i can reach the  middle split again by just doing a few  youtube tutorials and also going a  little bit more regularly to yoga and  dance classes  and then we'll see where i'm at at the  end of the week compared to the  beginning of the week  so yeah flexibility challenge day one  [Music]  okay  so this is day two of the middle split  challenge  and  um  yesterday went really bad actually i i  couldn't even reach the floor at all and  i can do the pancake on good days and i  used to be able to do the middle splits  but right now  during corona  i kinda  [ __ ] up everything  so i'm not able to do it anymore but  yeah we're first gonna do a little bit  of a warming up and then  i'm gonna do some simple stretches  ending with the middle split stretches  which are a lot more intense  so  warming up is important  that's that's my only advice yeah so  we're gonna try and see how that goes  and i'll link some videos that i usually  use when training for the middle split  um that i find really helpful  so you can try it as well at home if you  want to  [Music]  [Music]  so on average this week i stretched in  the morning for around 30 minutes and in  the evening around 30 minutes  and i wouldn't recommend stretching much  more as you could hurt yourself  otherwise and that's not what we want  then i usually use some yoga blocks to  support myself for deeper stretches a  foam roller for that really deep muscle  work  and a timer i set to 30 minutes  of course you also need your yoga mat  and some  loose clothing  and that's kind of it then it's just  basically consistency  and eventually you will get your splits  if you just do this for  in my case a week but perhaps for you it  will take a little bit longer  yeah enjoy the journey that's basically  my only advice  [Music]  so for the last two days i already felt  i was pretty close  and i think then most people have the  tendency to really push themselves into  it but don't do that i one time really  hurt myself and couldn't do the splits  for almost a year  so just relax and breathe and your body  will naturally go into the position  again  and also always keep your core tight  this just helps with general body  awareness and will disable you to really  hurt yourself  i also have some dips that i apply daily  to increase my flexibility and i think  following these will really help you  with overall body mobility  not just towards the splits but in  general  so i think one of the biggest things  with overall mobility is that most of us  just sit too much so i think  less sitting is one of the best things  you can do so for example just prop your  laptop up on a higher surface and use it  as a standing desk or every 60 minutes  for example stand up for five minutes  and just stretch a little bit this will  already help so much  so another big tip that i heard is this  so-called ground living so the idea is  that you just sit on the ground and you  kind of try to put yourself in natural  positions so this can be a lotus  position or just bending forward a  little bit and the idea is then that you  don't use furniture which in general is  just kind of bad for your back  and of course i do still use my desk  chair but one of the big things we have  to think about is posture just sit up  straight it's so important  so then another big one i heard is to  not use pillows and it depends a little  bit if you sleep on your side or back if  you sleep on your back though don't use  them it's just a bit better for the  general alignment of your body  so another big one is to try to stretch  during the day so whilst you do chores  for example like washing the dishes or  when you're brushing your  teeth to just bend forward  and try to touch the floor these kind of  little moments will add up in total  towards your overall flexibility  [Music]  and just try to move during the day so  take walks take the stairs etc and i  hope these kind of tips will help you  during the day and in general to  become more flexible  and hopefully reach the goals that you  want  [Music]  [Music]  okay so this is the last day of the  challenge so i kind of wanted to give a  little bit of the tips and tricks of  what i learned whilst doing this  challenge so here you can see how far i  actually got so i could finally reach  the floor again  after  one and a half years two years  and as i said before i could do the  pancake but now i could get my feet to  also stretch outward fully so one of the  things that i learned whilst doing this  challenge  and researching extremely flexible  people on youtube is that most of them  actually have a lifestyle that allows  them to be really flexible so for  example they're dancers or athletes  and then people like us look at them and  think like oh my god how can i become  like that  whilst we're just sitting at an office  job for eight hours a day so i think  whilst doing this challenge i kind of  realized  instead of these super intense  stretching routines that most people  follow it's actually  more important to kind of take a  holistic approach  where you also redesign your environment  to allow you to be more flexible so for  example  while sitting on the floor to stretch  forward or whilst watching tv to kind of  try to touch your toes  because these kind of little things that  you do during the day add up so much  more than if you just at the end of the  day do a super intense stretching  routine so one of the things i would  also recommend  is to work on your strength alongside  your flexibility because about five  years ago i injured myself really badly  by trying to go in the  sideward split  whilst i actually wasn't strong enough  so i really stretched every every day  and pushed myself really hard but i  actually didn't work on my strengths and  that kind of made me tear my limp which  um or tear my hamstring  which  is a super hard injury to recover from  it took me almost a year  and it was my right leg and my right leg  now is still my bad leg like stretching  wise and i really hope to kind of  continue this  stretching journey that i have been  doing for the last five days or this  routine because what i actually really  want to achieve is the needle as you can  see here and i'm still pretty far off  because my backbends aren't  super good and i also don't have enough  strength to kind of throw my leg up that  high  but i think i'll be working on it  through the weeks and perhaps around  december or something i will do another  little  week video um to show my progress  so i hope you guys also learned  something and perhaps also work on your  flexibility yourself because i would  love to hear how you guys work on your  flexibility increase it and how the  journey is for you in general so see you  soon  [Music]  you

